{
  "id": "A06",
  "goal": "S1-05A",
  "title": "The room's exchange with Sophia: its controls, Sophia's presence, and the private media-bridge service",
  "why": [
    "startExchange existed as a contract only. S1-05A opens it: one exchange per room, opened explicitly by a member (joining the room never opens it), with explicit End, Stop Speaking, Show Sophia this, Stop Looking and Resume. Each control moves an epoch (input, playback or observation) so late audio, frames or tool results of an older epoch are fenced, and none of them touches admitted work.",
    "Room gains `sophia`, the observed state of Sophia in this room: whether an exchange is open or paused and why, whether her voice is actually connected (as the media bridge last reported it, and unavailable when it stops reporting), whose input is admitted and what she is looking at. The Studio's light follows it instead of the LiveKit connection: a joined room is not evidence that Google hears anyone.",
    "The media bridge (apps/media-bridge) is a service principal with its own capability, like the runtime (A04). /v1/media/* gives it the exchanges to serve (with a short-lived LiveKit token as identity `sophia`), takes its presence reports and quiescence acknowledgements, clears a departed holder by compare-and-set, and executes Gemini tool calls for the speaker the input epoch binds, never for a name the model produced. It also lists background results finished during the exchange, which the bridge announces once at an idle boundary and records as announced.",
    "Viewers (A01 kept them listening) may now speak in the human room and hold the floor for a read-only exchange: talking with Sophia is not a work grant. Starting or controlling work still requires editor or admin at the tool call, exactly as over HTTP. This changes A01's behaviour, not its records; it is for Luis's review.",
    "Guests keep the human call (A02/A03) but never a project-aware Sophia: a guest present in the room pauses the exchange, the guest's token waits for the bridge to confirm Sophia stopped listening and speaking, and only explicit member action resumes her once the room is member-only again."
  ],
  "patch": [
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/components/securitySchemes/mediaBridgeCapability",
      "value": {
        "type": "http",
        "scheme": "bearer",
        "description": "The media bridge's capability: an opaque secret on the bridge host; the API holds only its SHA-256. It names no member and grants no member authority: tool calls act for the speaker the exchange's input epoch binds, under that speaker's own role."
      }
    },
